---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Musicals online"
  description="Musicals you can legally watch or hear at home: film versions, cast recordings and the clips productions publish themselves — and why full stage recordings are not linked here."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">At home</p>
    <h1>Musicals online</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A stage musical is not usually something you can stream. What exists
      legally is a film version, a cast recording, and whatever the
      production itself puts out — and that is what this page collects.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What is linked here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Official clips.</strong> Numbers a production or a broadcaster published on its own channel: award-show performances, trailers, rehearsal footage.</li>
      <li><strong>Film adaptations.</strong> Where a musical has one, on the services that actually licensed it.</li>
      <li><strong>Cast recordings.</strong> The original and revival albums, which for most shows are the only complete record of the score.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bootlegs and reuploads</strong> of full stage performances, however many views they have.</li>
      <li><strong>Aggregator pages</strong> that promise a stream and deliver a survey.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="note">
    <strong>Nothing is embedded here yet.</strong> Each clip is checked as an
    official upload before it goes on the page, and none has been checked yet.
    An empty section is better than a page of dead or infringing embeds.
  </Callout>
</Layout>
